<title>USA: Allegheny Cty, Pa., PA trims $197 mln from project.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Cty, Pa., PA trims $197 mln from project.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Allegheny County, Pa., Port Authority said it would trim about $197 million from a plan to improve access to the city's airport.</p>
<p>Executive Director Paul Skoutelas said the cost of the project, which originally envisioned building a buses-only roadway, has ballooned to more than $490 million, out of reach for the authority.</p>
<p>Skoutelas said the authority now plans to eliminate a custom bridge into downtown Pittsburgh and convert one lane of West Carson Street for bus use only.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
